VERDICT: STRONGLY-OPPOSES
  scope: Adversarial (opponent) assessment of the proposal to implement the corpus-index overhaul in archon-cli (Rust/CozoDB) rather than in
  scope: claudeflow-testing (Python compiler + TypeScript runtime). Read-only inspection of both repos on 2026-07-29: git history and branch/remote
  scope: topology in both; the four prior archon port/handoff/validation documents; the pre-existing corpus-index→archon migration spec; live archon
  scope: binary (1.3.11, 7b44c665) read-only subcommands; quote_verify.rs / archon-draft / archon-docs schema source; compile-corpus-index.py; live
  scope: npx tsc --noEmit; dissertation drafting file mtimes. No writes, no builds, no pushes.

  PORT COST:
      3–6 months of calendar time to reach the spec's own P5 parity gate, versus days for the cheap alternative. Three independent bases.  BASIS 1 —
      the repo's own build-ready spec. `plans/archon-corpus-index-migration-spec.md:130-142` sizes this exact migration at nine phases: P0=M, P0.5=L,
      P1=L, P2=M, P3=L, P4=M, P5=XL, P6=M, P7=M — one XL, three L, five M. P5 is "Datalog retriever to PARITY — 3 blocks + mandatory bridge, exact
      templates/caps/scorers, line-for-line diff vs live TS as the HARD gate." The spec was written against "~19 hand-authored entries"; there are now
      27 (+42%), 1,759 files, 39 MB (`find corpus/index -type f -not -path '*/.backups/*' | wc -l` → 1759).  BASIS 2 — observed archon delivery rate
      on a comparable item in an ALREADY-ported crate. V-3/V-4 quote verification was scoped "M–L" in archon-ingestion-port-finish-
      plan-2026-06-30.md:217-218. It first landed 2026-07-01 (00d01f0e) and required six more commits through 2026-07-16 (a3126b02, b425789d,
      5589ec30, e4b25301, 2bf98d8a, 849eadfc) — 15 days elapsed for 596 lines — and is still incomplete on three axes (offsets discarded at
      quote_verify.rs:405; REPORT_FLOOR=0.60 ungated at :20; archon-draft has no archon-docs dependency so the drafting path cannot call it). If one
      M–L item costs ~15 days elapsed and lands incomplete, five M + three L + one XL across a subsystem with zero existing substrate is
      conservatively 3–6 months — and that assumes a nonzero cadence, whereas the observed cadence for the last 11 days is zero commits.  BASIS 3 —
      prior port completion record. ARCHON-PORT2-COMPLETE-2026-06-25.md declared the ingestion port complete, then documents 21 adversarial findings
      (17 confirmed, 7 substantive fixed) at :70-88 and a "NOT implemented (out of scope, tracked)" list at :102-106; HANDOFF-archon-ingestion-
      port-2026-07-01.md:92-111 still carried a five-item queue six days later.  CHEAP ALTERNATIVE COST — days, all in the existing split. (a)
      QuoteFragment gains char_start/char_end: struct at quote_verify.rs:33-42, literal at :405-411; `local_range: Option<(usize,usize)>` is already a
      parameter at :371 and destructured at :374 — ~4 lines. (b) Verification gate keyed on match_kind: `MatchKind::{Exact,Fuzzy}` already exists at
      :26-29 — one match arm. (c) compile-corpus-index.py:718-721 elif reorder — 4 lines, fixes the last-field-absorbs-the-file pollution. (d) Add
      "index" to SKIP_DIRS at run_ingest.py:365, run_ingest_phase2.py:978, parallel_ingest.py:69 — 3 tokens, stops 518 of 522 index manifest records
      re-embedding into the live corpus.

  SUMMARY:
      The strongest case against archon-first does not rest on Rust being worse. It rests on four verified facts.  First, a build-ready,
      adversarially-reviewed spec for this exact port already exists and has produced nothing. `plans/archon-corpus-index-migration-spec.md`
      (2026-06-24) specs corpus/index → archon Cozo across nine phases and was endorsed "high confidence." Thirty-five days later `grep -rn
      'corpus_entries|corpus_concepts|ensure_corpus_schema' crates/` returns empty and archon's 942 MB store holds 227 documents, all PDFs, zero index
      entries. The spec's own framing is the decisive line: "The substrate is the easy part; ADAPTER COVERAGE is the long pole. The build is gated not
      by CozoDB mechanics (verified trivial) but by the heterogeneity of ~19 hand-authored entries." Cozo and Rust buy nothing on the critical path;
      the long pole is irregular hand-authored markdown, which is where Rust is slowest and where the 231-agent review explicitly recommended KEEPING
      the five Python parsers.  Second, the two-repo split is not a hypothetical cost — it has already happened and already silently lost data.
      `archon-cli/index/` is a checked-in duplicate of `corpus/index/` (1,731 tracked files). It is missing three entire entries — Presence Theory
      (Foundations), Rhetoric of Interactivity and VR (Part III), Social Presence in Virtual Worlds (Part III), 25 files — and its `compiled-
      index.json` is 643,548 bytes from Jul 16 against the incumbent's 664,494 from Jul 20, different md5. Sync is manual (`chore(index): commit
      compiled research index as a working data asset`). Archon-first makes the authoring side permanently remote from the compiler.  Third, archon
      has no delivery capacity and a poor completion record. HEAD 8758f2fa is on no remote at all — `git branch -r --contains` returns empty — with
      186 commits unlanded and origin/main frozen since 2026-06-13. Last archon commit was 2026-07-18, eleven days ago. Meanwhile dissertation
      drafting ran 26 files on 07-29 and 6 on 07-28. Port #2 was declared COMPLETE on 06-25, then an adversarial review found 21 defects (17
      confirmed, 7 substantive, including a byte-vs-code-point token estimator that shifted every chunk boundary on the Greek corpus), and a five-item
      queue was still open on 07-01. The comparable V-3/V-4 quote matcher, scoped "M–L," took 7 commits across 15 days and is still incomplete on
      three axes.  Fourth, the cheapest thing that works is genuinely days, not months, and the usual justification for porting does not survive
      inspection. `npx tsc --noEmit` does report 157 errors — but zero of them are in the four index-consuming modules; they are concentrated in
      section-orchestrator (26) and __experimental__ (45). The index layer being overhauled is type-clean. The highest-value fixes are tiny:
      reordering two elif arms at compile-corpus-index.py:718-721 kills the pollution that has one centralityTier holding 10,009 chars; adding "index"
      to three SKIP_DIRS sets stops 518 index manifest records being re-embedded; and adding char_start/char_end to QuoteFragment is a four-line
      change because local_range is already in scope at quote_verify.rs:371 and thrown away at :405.  The honest caveat: archon's capabilities are
      real. doc_chunk_blocks carries char offsets, quote_verify resolves sub-span page and bbox, archon-evidence/index.rs is 977 working lines. But
      archon-draft — where the drafting protocol actually pulls quotations — has no dependency on archon-docs and therefore cannot call locate_quote
      at all. Two components in the same repo, still unconnected after 15 days of work. That argues for calling archon as a verification service from
      the incumbent, not for relocating the overhaul into it.

