VERDICT: FAVOURS
  scope: True state of the evidence-curation work in archon-cli: full read of crates/archon-evidence/ (lib.rs, index.rs, pack.rs, verify.rs,
  scope: quote_trim.rs, outcome.rs = 3,112 lines), its CLI surface (src/command/evidence.rs, curate.rs, curate_agent.rs, evidence_view.rs,
  scope: evidence_index.rs = 2,619 lines), its TUI record types, git log on feat/evidence-curation, and a re-test of the six CRITICALs and the
  scope: "declarative pipeline non-functional" finding from the 2026-07-13 adversarial review against current HEAD (8758f2fa). Live read-only runs of
  scope: `archon docs status`, `archon evidence find --json`, `archon docs verify-quote --json` against .archon/archon-data.db. Plan documents read:
  scope: plans/index-entry-creation-plan-CLAIM-LEVEL-2026-07-29.md §§0-5 and the memory record project-archon-adversarial-review-results.md (the
  scope: RESULTS .md itself exists only in git history at b0a29a50, not on disk). Not in scope / not done: no cargo build or test, no write
  scope: operations, no assessment of the TypeScript runtime beyond one spot-check.

  PORT COST:
      Two separable pieces, sized against measured prior work in this repo. (1) The parts that already exist need no port at all: the clause layer,
      the verification gate and the index reader are shipped, merged into HEAD and CI-tested; exposing the offsets is ~25-40 lines (P19). (2) The
      compiler/authoring adapter has no Rust counterpart and must be built: ~1,900 lines of source to replace (~1,100 of compile-corpus-index.py's
      1,412 plus ~600 of cross-author-utils.ts and 202 of corpus-index-provider.ts). Basis for the expansion factor: the FCDP port removed 891 lines
      of Python across 7 files (365be93b) and added 2,497 lines of Rust including tests and fixtures (8bfe441d), both landed 2026-07-08 alongside the
      crate scaffold f8779fd1 — 2.8x lines, ~1 day. That projects to ~4,500-5,500 Rust lines for the compiler, i.e. one crate of roughly archon-
      evidence's size. Basis for the schedule: archon-evidence itself went from crate creation (c98aca59, 2026-07-10) to hardened-and-committed
      (2bf98d8a, 2026-07-14) — 3,112 lines of crate source plus 2,619 lines of bin modules plus TUI screens, 56 tests, in 5 days. archon-lanham (2,461
      lines) was ported in a comparable window (f637a00c, 2026-06-25). So: compiler port ≈ 1-2 weeks at the observed pace, plus the CozoDB record
      schema and validator (~600-900 lines, ~3-5 days). The ~40-field CLAIM model, the five sibling record types and the migration of ~5,000 authored
      records are NOT port cost — they are new construction that costs the same in either repo. The genuine archon-vs-claudeflow differential is
      therefore the compiler (a real net cost in archon) against the corpus store, addressing, verification gate, tested index reader and CI (all real
      net costs in claudeflow, and one of them — re-ingesting 226 PDFs to recover per-block char offsets and bboxes — is by far the largest single
      item on either side).

  SUMMARY:
      The evidence-curation work is real, shipped, merged and tested — it is not a prototype. `archon evidence curate` today runs an agentic research
      assistant that may only select retrieved spans by id, then produces two files: pack.json and quotes.json. Its record shape is quote-centric —
      QuoteIndexEntry {id, source, locus, description, intended_use} joined positionally to QuoteEntry {text, cite} and EvidenceItem {id, grade,
      content}. Something already resembles a claim record with a locus: ReviewItem (crates/archon-tui/src/screens/evidence_curation_util.rs:62-91)
      carries a one-line claim, a locus, a cite, page, bbox, chunk_id and every located page-box — but it is transient, and NOTHING from a curation is
      ever written to the store. verify.rs re-verifies each bank quote against the live corpus scoped to the document the pack cites, classifies it
      Exact/NearVerbatim/Drift/Missing/WrongSource, and blocks every non-exact status. On the 2026-07-13 review: all six CRITICALs are fixed and on
      the current branch — CR-1/CR-2 by an exact-only delete/reprocess resolver with --all-matching opt-in and two named regression tests, CR-3 by
      source-scoped verify_bank plus the WrongSource class, CR-4 by gating the 2-up remap on a genuine-2-up check, CR-5 by reading
      manifest.vector_count in snapshot_is_current plus snapshot invalidation and auto-rebuild, CR-6 by replacing the sticky latch with an expiring
      cooldown. feat/evidence-curation (2bf98d8a) is an ancestor of HEAD 8758f2fa, so none of this is stranded. The separate "declarative pipeline run
      non-functional" finding is STILL TRUE and untouched since 2026-05-08. On the sizing question: roughly the clause layer, the addressing, the
      verification gate and a tested index reader are already built in archon — the corpus is live at 226 documents / 17,824 chunks with per-block
      char offsets and bboxes, while claudeflow's .archon is 28 KB and empty. What is NOT built in archon is the whole authoring side: no index
      compiler exists there at all (its index/ is a hand-copied, already-drifted snapshot), no claim/clause/edge/tension/term/source relations exist,
      no validator, and no persistence for anything a curation produces. That splits cleanly: everything downstream of the record already favours
      archon and would have to be rebuilt or re-ingested to move to claudeflow; everything upstream of the record is a genuine net cost in archon,
      estimated at one crate of archon-evidence's size (~4,500-5,500 Rust lines, 1-2 weeks at this repo's measured pace). The honest recommendation
      the evidence supports is archon-first for the store, schema, addressing and verification, with the five markdown parsers kept where the review
      put them — as adapters emitting a typed intermediate — rather than ported wholesale.

